{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/15540-what-is-mummy-about","id":15540,"title":"What is Mummy about?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-21T12:45:51-08:00","id":15540,"title":"What is Mummy about?","content":"I'm trying to decide whether Mummy is worth buying... And I was wondering: what is, exactly, this game about?<br /> <br /> I mean: Vampire is about politics. Changeling is about hiding from True Fae and rebuilding your life. Hunter is about investigating and / or hunting the supernatural. What is Mummy about?<br /> <br /> From what I've read online, this game seems to be about relic-hunting. Isn't this a bit limited?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:10:10-08:00","id":15559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/15540-what-is-mummy-about#post15540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I've read online, this game seems to be about relic-hunting. Isn't this a bit limited?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is somewhat wrong. It's actually about memory and self discovery. Relics are mostly just a tool to jag a mummy's memory banks in an effort to get them to realize who they were.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:11:36-08:00","id":15561,"title":"","content":"Mummy is about secrets. Your past is a secret. Your mission is a secret. The way out is a secret. Relic-hunting and cult management is the everyday experience, at least to start, but the meat of the game's character focus is in discovering who you were and are, what you've done, what's been done to you, and what you can do about it. It's about secrets to the extent that half the book is recommended not to be read by players.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The titular curse of Mummy is the condition of the Arisen: the same rite that grants them eternal life traps them as eternal servants of selfish, parasitic gods. The demands of Memory are at odds with the demands of the Descent. There is a way out of this condition, to seize control of the rite for yourself, but it's a personal journey to seek.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Personally, it's not my bag and I would pump money into the Demon Kickstarter instead, but I think that's a fair shake, thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T17:16:28-08:00","id":15716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/15540-what-is-mummy-about?p=15561#post15561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy is about secrets. Your past is a secret. Your mission is a secret. The way out is a secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I don't quite get it. Surely a player knows the most important things about the game when it begins - if not, how can this player even create a character? The player knows that he's going to play a mummy from an ancient empire. What secret is there, then?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T20:31:17-08:00","id":15834,"title":"","content":"Who the character really is, what they might have done the last time they were called upon by their cult. I read an AP awhile ago that illustrated it nicely. One of the players was finding his cult, and as he found them, began recalling memories of punishing them brutally. They also found out that all the other Arisen in the city were afraid of one of the other PCs, because he'd built some structure which sucked the life out of people.<br /> <br /> The mystery is in fulfilling your obligation to cult and Judge while discovering who you are, and what you'll do with that knowledge of yourself. All of that within the time frame of before you have to go back to sleep again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T20:41:06-08:00","id":15843,"title":"","content":"I have some song entries to write alongside a shower I desperately need before, but I want to say this:<br /> <br /> Mummy is a game about fighting time, in every sense of the phrase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T22:25:33-08:00","id":15891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/15540-what-is-mummy-about#post15540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to decide whether Mummy is worth buying... And I was wondering: what is, exactly, this game about?<br /> <br /> I mean: Vampire is about politics. Changeling is about hiding from True Fae and rebuilding your life. Hunter is about investigating and / or hunting the supernatural. What is Mummy about?<br /> <br /> From what I've read online, this game seems to be about relic-hunting. Isn't this a bit limited?</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely you agree that it's a bad idea to ignore 95% of a game like Vampire and reduce it to the point of &quot;Vampire is a game about politics&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the same sense, Mummy is a game about a great many things, memory and relic hunting and the experience of old age and losing one's strength and nostalgia and the dangers thereof among them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T23:10:02-08:00","id":15918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/15540-what-is-mummy-about?p=15716#post15716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit I don't quite get it. Surely a player knows the most important things about the game when it begins - if not, how can this player even create a character? The player knows that he's going to play a mummy from an ancient empire. What secret is there, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything else.<br /> <br /> What happened last time you awoke, the time before that and the hundreds of times before that. You see someone, another Arisen, you get a surge of positive emotion but no idea why. You have a dozen fearful mortals at your feet worshipping you...it's wrong...there should be more, at least, you think so.<br /> <br /> You've got &gt;6000 years of history as a PC, you remember snippets of 6000 years ago (very small snippets at that) and maybe a dozen facts about yourself for the 6000 years between then and now.<br /> <br /> Problem is other people remember a hell of a lot more than you do...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T00:37:51-08:00","id":15941,"title":"","content":"I couldn't agree more, Scutarii. It's a game about the terrifying nature of memory loss, lack of self-identity and purpose, and the discovery of all of these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T12:26:23-08:00","id":16227,"title":"","content":"I see. Hmm.<br /> <br /> Anything else this game could be about? Tell me everything <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T21:10:02-08:00","id":16451,"title":"","content":"the game could be encompassed by describing how it is sort of a metaphor for old age. you remember that you were once glorious--you long for the olden days, even if you don't remember them. you reminisce, trying desperately to grasp at fading threads and vanishing memories. many of the people you loved are already dead, or will soon die, including other immortals. when your friends are slowly fading and your what legacy will you leave behind for your followers? where will you lay your body to rest? do you trust those around you to take care of you when you are weak and can no longer support yourself? are you the same person, now, that you used to be? did you accomplish anything important that youve forgotten? have you done things that you now regret? what can you still do, now, to make a difference? is the afterlife you have been promised, been waiting for all your life, really there, or something you want? where did you put that thing you loved so much? how do you deal with changes to the world you just can't understand? and, really, with all of this to worry about.. was it worth it to live so long, or would it have been better to simply have died long ago? sucks getting old, doesn't it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T22:54:05-08:00","id":16478,"title":"","content":"Mummy is about being exploited. You've been compelled to do the bidding of Judges of the Underworld, and you can't even die to escape your servitude. You've been trained to think this exploitation is good - noble, even. You're in command of a cult - or they're in command of you. You can take time out of your job to try to reclaim your identity, but those below do not approve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T07:27:44-08:00","id":16632,"title":"","content":"Thanks again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And, if we were to speak of specific stories / plots? What could Mummy story involve, aside from relic hunting and cult managing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T09:28:17-08:00","id":16668,"title":"","content":"Your Guild Hierarch is in a vulnerable state, out of favour with the majority but supported and propped up by a clique of high ranked individuals. They have begun lashing out at anyone who seems to be building popular support or threats of a coup to remove them. Things have grown to a head of late as rumours of a senior Scribe coming to your Nome are circulating, the incumbent is worried this is a precursor to an attempt to send them to Obloquy.<br /> <br /> This process has been going on across the span of a century and your PCs have found themselves awakening within it, unsure of their previous involvement, which side they were on, who supports what position, etc. You have to find some way of untangling the threads of politics and power and where you and everyone else fit in before someone else casts you as friend or foe to either side takes action to shatter any powerbase you may have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T15:49:37-08:00","id":17985,"title":"","content":"One huge specific story element ive been using a ton is flashbacks. Hell, because of the playstyle and storyline of the Mummy crossover ive been running, the majority of the events are actually flashbacks as his Memory grows. Setting events in the past is perfect for Mummy, because a) you can be killed, youll just come back, so there is still danger.. and b) with faulty memory, you dont really need to figure out how much your character does or doesnt know at the time. Mummy is great for flashback scenes to important plot points or NPCs--so long as they are appropriate to his Memory score and to the mystery of forgetfulness that gives mummy its horror edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T09:57:56-08:00","id":18479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/15540-what-is-mummy-about?p=15941#post15941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't agree more, Scutarii. It's a game about the terrifying nature of memory loss, lack of self-identity and purpose, and the discovery of all of these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very nicely &amp; succintly put.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T13:36:52-08:00","id":18683,"title":"","content":"See, this is exactly why I wish every splat corebook had an appendix that explained this sort of thing clearly. I hate to admit this, because I consider myself an intelligent person, and this makes me feel a little dumb, but I'm the type who is pretty literalist in his reading. I'd read the mechanics of the splat, and just come away with &quot;this is how they work, these are the things they can do&quot;, and will completely miss the poetic subtextual statements that went into them! Like all the stuff about Mummyism (not a word, I'm sure) being a metaphor for old age, that probably would never have occurred to me on finishing the book...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So now I'm wondering what other subtexts I'm missing in other games (I know this has been a problem with some of the more esoteric material in Exalted, such as Sidereals). Anyway, thanks for helping another guy get his head around The Curse, it sounds much more interesting now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}